# Image Handling Rules

## Source/reference image is read-only

The project contains a read-only source/reference image used as the baseline for kernel development, testing, and comparison.

The source/reference image is strictly immutable.

NEVER:

* modify its contents;
* delete, create, or overwrite files or directories inside it;
* truncate, recreate, or otherwise alter the image itself;
* use it as a writable workspace;
* mount or manipulate it in a way that could modify its contents.

The source/reference image must remain exactly as provided.

## Copy-on-Write workflow

Whenever an image needs to be modified for development, testing, packaging, or experimentation:

1. Create a writable Copy-on-Write (CoW) copy of the source/reference image.
2. Perform all modifications exclusively on the writable CoW image.
3. Use the CoW image for all destructive operations, temporary changes, kernel deployment, and testing.
4. Never modify the original source/reference image.

The original source/reference image must remain available as an untouched baseline from which new CoW images can be created.

## Image identification

Before performing any operation that may modify an image, the agent MUST determine whether the target is:

* the immutable source/reference image; or
* a writable CoW/test image.

If there is any uncertainty about which image is being modified, STOP and resolve the ambiguity before making changes.

## Priority

These rules apply to all Cursor Agent work in this repository and should be followed in every session.

Any future user instruction that explicitly changes or supersedes these rules may update the workflow, but the source/reference image must remain protected unless the user explicitly authorizes modifying it.
